  "rationale": "The workflow already includes a job-level timeout (10 minutes) which aligns with the P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT pattern's mechanism of bounding jobs with a custom timeout. The available history shows only two successful runs (~9 seconds each), which is insufficient to establish a representative duration distribution for safely reducing the timeout. The pattern's preconditions require a representative successful-duration history, and its safety tests include validating against slow valid runs. Without more data, reducing the timeout risks false failures. No other patterns (e.g., caching, matrix fail-fast, stale cancellation) apply to this single-job, manual-dispatch publish workflow. Therefore, no evidence-supported change is warranted.",
